 "text": "Hi, how have you been? The SSD stores data in flash memory, which is fast but expensive, while a hard drive uses spinning disks, is cheaper but slower. Yes, an SSD makes your computer feel much faster, especially when starting up or switching applications. Going from traditional hard drive to SSD feels like going from crawling to running, so it' worth it. Cloud storage is great for backing up and sharing files, but nothing beats having your data on fast storage in your own house.",
